  {
   "type": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "India's densest forests, such as the tropical moist forest of the Andaman Islands, the Western Ghats, and Northeast India, occupy about 3% of its land area."
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "According to the IUCN Red List, India contains 1,021 threatened animal species—99 mammal, 82 bird, 105 reptile, 139 amphibian, 332 fish, 10 mollusk, and 254 other invertebrate —727 threatened plant species, and 4 threatened fungi species."
