  {
   "type": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Cabinet: Officially known in India as the Union Council of Ministers, the Cabinet is the principal institution of governance."
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Political parties: Since the mid-1980s—marking the second half of India's postcolonial history—the Bharatiya Janata Party, or BJP, has grown from a marginal party into a political giant."
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "From the late 1980s to 2014, local or regional parties wielded heavy clout nationwide by anchoring coalition governments and holding the keys to making or breaking central rule."
  },
  {
